  "definition": "Action Upon Filing of Application for Crossing License",
  "effectiveDate": "2024-04-26",
  "historyNote": "#13939, eff 4-26-24",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "En 1504.01",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1500.html",
  "prefLabel": "En 1504.01 Action Upon Filing of Application for Crossing License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1504.01 Action Upon Filing of Application for Crossing License.\n\n(a) The department shall assign a number to each application and upon review shall communicate with the applicant regarding any perceived omissions or other defects, as well as regarding any questions and any perceived grounds for denial.\n\n(b) The department shall condition any license issued under this paragraph in any manner necessary to assure that the license is likely to be exercised safely so as to avoid substantially affecting the public rights in public waters or state-owned lands.\n\n(c) Using a non-adjudicative process, the department of energy shall reject incomplete or improperly filed applications unless an application is cured upon request by the department, and shall, also using a non-adjudicative process, issue or deny the license within 90 days of receiving a complete application and all information subsequently requested of an applicant.\n\nSource. #13939, eff 4-26-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1500.html"
}
